      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/pygocentrus_nattereri_small_spots_en/",
      "html": "<p>The Red Piranha, Pygocentrus nattereri, is the only species of piranha that is bred on a commercial basis due to the high demand on these fishes in the ornamental fish trade. So it is always available in the shops and almost all of the offered fish are bred ones.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/09-characoids-tetra-relationship/pygocentrus_nattereri_small_spots_en/",
      "html": "<p>Wild collected specimens of an extremely pretty and colourful local variety of P. nattereri, called “Small Spots”, were imported. The fish originate from the area around the city of Manacapuru (catchment of the Rio Negro), Brazil.</p>"
    }
